# D-SOLE-SURVIVOR-CREATES-FAIL-EBUSY-FROM-DIALLOC-AFTER-PEER-FENCE: after H-EB1
# was REFUTED (tests/queues/ebusy_retire_first_ab.queue: neither injected control
# reproduced the double grant), does EBUSY still occur on this build at all?
# Same build as that queue's default laps ebd1-ebd8 (~/src/mxfs-g
# 65863B924040AF5213F2A76, 0 EBUSY in 8 with dl_import_retire_first=1), now with
# dl_import_retire_first=0 and no injection: the build's behaviour without the
# H-EB1 change.  Run from ~/src/mxfs-g.  2/net/mesh/mpath g2e (test17 test18);
# path_fenced_return fences test18, test17 survives and creates; then
# chk_clean.  Natural rate before (chain pfi, an older build, same rows and
# group): EBUSY creates on test17 in 3 of 8 laps, each with a
# P-TAUTH-DOUBLE-GRANT against the fenced node's EX record on an AG page.
#
# READING RULES (written before the first lap): per lap, 'ERR EBUSY' lines in
# load_test17/ops.log, P-TAUTH-DOUBLE-GRANT lines naming the fenced test18
# incarnation in either capture, row 'fence: no operation on test17 returned an
# error', chk_clean's verdict, knobs.txt read back on both nodes (a lap whose
# knobs did not take judges nothing).
#   REPRODUCES: at least one lap with EBUSY on test17; those laps' own lines
#     then carry the next hypothesis.
#   ABSENT ON THIS BUILD: 0 EBUSY and 0 P-TAUTH-DOUBLE-GRANT in all 8: H-EB1's
#     change is not what removed it, and the change since the pfi build that
#     did is to be found (bisect the pfi build against this one) before any
#     disposition; a clean run is not one.
#   Any shutdown, BUG, Oops, hung task or chk_clean not CLEAN is attributed from
#   its own lines first; the typeflip ESTALE shape (test18's mkdir ESTALE after
#   rejoining) belongs to D-CAW-MKDIR-LOOKUP-ESTALE-TYPEFLIP-UNRESOLVED.
#
# Bounds: as tests/queues/ebusy_retire_first_ab.queue (same rows, same group):
# path_fenced_return 400 s + chk_clean 180 s + the chain's measured overhead
# outside the rows (130-160 s) = 730 s; the first lap adds prep_cluster 300 s.
